 2.  **ToF Rendering:**
     $$L_{\text{ToF}}(\mathbf{x}, \boldsymbol{\omega}_0, \tau) = \int_{t_n}^{t_f} \frac{T^{\text{blend}}(\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{x}_t, \tau)^2}{\|\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{x}_t\|^2} \sigma^{\text{blend}}(\mathbf{x}_t, \tau) I_s^{\text{blend}}(\mathbf{x}_t, \boldsymbol{\omega}_0, \tau) W(2 \|\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{x}_t\|) dt$$
-    Where $W(\cdot)$ is the system's point spread function (PSF) or weighting function, and the term $\frac{1}{\|\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{x}_t\|^2}$ accounts for distance attenuation [S2, unofficial]. The integral limits $t_n$ and $t_f$ represent the near and far clipping planes of the ray [S2, unofficial].
